<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Razakars (Hyderabad)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1946">1946</a>–<a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Razakars were a paramilitary force of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/all-india-majlis-e-ittehadul-muslimeen">Majlis-e-Ittehadul Muslimeen</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a> State, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qasim-razvi">Qasim Razvi</a>, that opposed the state's accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. In 1947-1948 they carried out attacks on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindus</a> and on opponents of the Nizam's regime. Their violence was one reason for India's military action, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/operation-polo">Operation Polo</a>, in September 1948, after which they were disbanded.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/razakars-hyderabad.jpg" alt="Razakars (Hyderabad)" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Razakar_units_being_trained_from_Muslim_volunteers.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
